WEBVTT

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.080
Gil made his move!

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.750
His poisonous claws ripped out
our souls! Gah! He's too good!

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:21.250
Kosame took a bullet for Appare
but the bleeding won't stop!

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.950
Shit! There's no future for us!

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:56.580
Kosame!

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.580
Open your eyes, Kosame!

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:01.700
What have you done?! Hey! Kosame!

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.790
No luck! The cars won't start!

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.000
This can't be... Kosame...

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.580
If we don't get him to a hospital...
There's too much blood.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.660
--I'll carry him!
--I'll help!

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.120
You can't! It'll take too long!

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.500
Besides, if we don't stop the bleeding,
he won't make it there.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:26.290
Then what do we do?!
I... At this rate, Kosame...

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.120
Keep pressure on it!

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:34.620
Calm down, Appare.
I don't know what to do either.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.200
Hey!

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.700
What's goin' on?

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:48.410
Chase! Lend us a hand!

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.120
"Episode 11: Rain in the Dark Night"

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.000
"Episode 11: Rain in the Dark Night"
I removed the bullet and
stitched up the wound, but...

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.000
I removed the bullet and
stitched up the wound, but...

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:01.290
...he lost so much blood, it's questionable
whether he'll wake or not.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.580
Does he have family we can contact?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:10.200
Kosame's family is far away.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.660
In the Far East, across the sea.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:16.000
I see.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.160
Why?

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.450
Why?! Why did you do something like that?!

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.580
This... isn't logical.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.200
Appare!

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.450
Shouldn't you be at his side?

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.040
How will that help?

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.450
Huh?

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.450
I'm... totally useless.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.790
Let's get all the cars inspected.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:25.700
I want to know the damage,
but we'll be lucky if the race goes on.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.620
I'll make an announcement
to the media tomorrow morning--

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.790
Mr. Carter!

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.830
Mr. Lyon.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.950
I'm sorry to hear about Sofia.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:38.290
Yeah... I need to fix my car over here.

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.830
Sure. That's fine with me, but...

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:45.330
Hurry up! It doesn't have to
be perfect! Just get it to run!

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:46.660
Yes, sir!

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.620
I'm asking the police to help with the search.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.000
I'm sure we'll locate the train, but...

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.200
...seeing how it's Gil,
we can't just rush to the rescue.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.580
I'll rescue her myself then.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:00.950
But...!

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:05.790
Appare!

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.660
How's Kosame?

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:12.200
"Questionable." That's what the doctor said.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.120
I see.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:19.700
Your machine's in bad shape, too.
It'll take a while to fix.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.290
I won't fix it.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:23.750
Huh? Why not?

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:27.290
Making something like this was pointless.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:31.120
The race is just like Kosame said--

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:35.200
"Driving at ridiculous speeds
for no good reason."

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.040
And now this...

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.330
Snap out of it, Appare!

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:43.580
I need to fix my car to save Sofia!

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.660
Can you help me out?

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:46.950
Impossible.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:49.830
I can't do it.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.410
I'm so damn weak.

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:12.790
You only just noticed?

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:19.870
Tsk. You're the last person I wanna see.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:23.580
Laugh if you wanna,
but I ain't gonna thank you for--

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:25.830
He knocked me out, too.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.660
While you were out like a light, that is.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:35.080
When he stole my photo
of Claudia, I lost my mind.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.160
Claudia, huh?

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.580
That's why I told you--
that woman makes you weak.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:10.700
Don't speak ill of Claudia!

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.200
I'm talking shit about you.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:18.330
You never deserved a woman as incredible as her.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.830
What if, back then...

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:25.040
If you had won and stolen her away,

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.500
Claudia might still be alive today.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.370
Don't insult her like that!

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:36.540
Our duel had nothing
to do with it! She picked you!

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:44.370
Not even seeing that much is why
you lost your mind over a little photo.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.200
Maybe.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.370
Tsk!

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.750
'Sup!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.120
How is he?

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.830
I don't know.

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:10.950
I see.

00:08:10.950 --> 00:08:15.120
Here, eat up. You should get some rest, too.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:21.200
Kosame saved my life.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.950
So I'm staying right here till he wakes up.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:46.200
Hey! Hey, hey!

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.910
Aren't you here to visit him?

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:52.000
No. I was just passing by.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.500
Huh?

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:57.450
How will being there help? It's pointless.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.200
Probably.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:04.830
If you go there with a face that gloomy,
it'll hurt more than help.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:09.660
Here, eat. It's hard to think straight
on an empty stomach.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:10.910
I don't wanna.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.330
You a spoiled brat or something?!

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:17.040
"I don't wanna eat" ain't in our vocabulary!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:21.200
There's food to eat or there ain't!
Eat every chance you can!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:25.580
That's the code of us outlaws.
And don't you forget...

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.620
Huh?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.040
What an idiot.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:35.870
Yes. As far as we know,
there's three hostages, including the woman.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:37.750
A GM and Iron Motor VIP--

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:41.620
I'm not mobilizing the entire force
over three people!

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.450
But...!

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:45.290
Didn't B.I.G. BOSS
bring in the Thousand Three

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:48.870
and tell us police
not to interfere with 'em?!

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:50.790
But the situation's different--

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:54.830
I'm doing everything I can!
We're short-staffed here.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:10:00.410
I'm not taking on Gil the Butcher
only to blow it. My reputation's at stake.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.540
I don't give a damn about reputation!

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.450
It's the report you wanted.

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:16.040
I can see that. Assemble the racers, please.
We have a decision to make.

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.160
Yes, sir.

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:23.950
Shit!

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:26.540
Did you get the parts?!

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:29.700
Someone lend a hand over here!

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:33.790
Mr. Lyon. The brake drum broke
but we don't have parts.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:36.250
Just make it work. I don't care how.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:37.950
But without the parts--

00:10:37.950 --> 00:10:42.040
Then forget the damn brakes! It just has to run!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.120
Um, sorry...

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.950
Send someone to GM and see if
they have anything we can use.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:51.120
Yes, sir.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:57.330
Appare...

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.370
What would you do?

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:16.580
Is this the end?

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.000
Appare...

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:27.750
Appare...

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:53.580
What is... this feeling?

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.700
What's happened to me?

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:01.750
My mind's gone dark and I can't see a thing...

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.750
What am I... supposed I do?

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:16.700
What... can I even do?

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:30.750
Tell me, Kosame...

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.910
Hey, Appare! Try to get some rest!

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:50.950
Don't say that, Appare.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.160
You're amazing, you know.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.290
Appare! You better finish that!

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.290
Let's just continue the race.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:13:00.160
We do lots of things that don't make sense.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:32.910
Appare!

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.290
Appare!

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.040
Appare!

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:50.120
Appare! Kosame is...!

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.330
Kosame!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:16.750
Well? Did I trick you?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.250
Thank goodness! You're awake!

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.410
No reaction, huh? Argh!

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:24.750
Don't do anything. Just try to rest.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.450
My throat's all dry.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:27.870
I'll get water!

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.870
Yeah, thanks.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:34.250
Kosame.

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.700
Hmm?

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:39.000
I'm sorry. Because of me...

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:42.000
Don't apologize. It's bad luck.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:46.660
I'll heal in no time.
Besides, it's not your fault.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.000
But...

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:52.370
I wish you'd apologize
for lots of other stuff first.

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.290
Huh?

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:58.200
In times like this,
you're supposed to say "thanks."

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:02.580
Thanks.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:06.790
"Thanks, Kosame. From now on,
I'll do whatever you ask."

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:08.580
Don't push your luck.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:15.620
I'll settle for that.
How's the car? Can you fix it?

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:18.160
No... I don't know...

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:24.040
Seriously? You didn't ditch me here
to go work on the car?

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:28.500
Kosame... What should I do?

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:34.160
Hey, hey, what's with you?
Did the rain turn into snow or something?

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:39.910
Everyone's cars are a wreck
and Sofia was taken by Gil...

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:43.370
The race will probably get canceled.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.660
I see.

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:50.330
Kosame, I'll build a ship to cross the Pacific.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.450
Huh? What are you on about?

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:56.870
If the race gets canceled,
we won't get any prize money.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.500
Don't you miss Japan? It'll take time, but--

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.620
You don't have to do that.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:07.790
There's plenty of steamboats I can take
if I want to cross the ocean, right?

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:12.870
If I miss Japan, I can find a job
and pay the fare myself.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:15.580
Besides, check it out, Appare.

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:21.580
This "blood transfusion" works if you have
the same blood type as someone.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:25.290
People out there are
thinking of incredible things.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:29.080
If it wasn't for this, I would've died.

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:35.500
You see, Appare? Remember what Gil said?
That nobody can stop him...

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:40.040
But we did. This technology stopped his power.

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:46.500
Appare... How far can you go?

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:51.330
Don't let someone else
decide the answer for you.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:52.700
Right?

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:56.410
Yeah.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.410
He can't stop me.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:04.450
That's the spirit. The Appare I know
will finish even if the race gets canceled.

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:06.200
That's just who you are.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:12.450
Appare. You might wanna know
the racers are assembling.

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.700
You need to get rest today.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:19.160
Even though you woke up,
your condition is far from good.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:21.290
You're an amazing guy.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:22.160
Huh?

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:23.410
Take care of 'em.

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:25.000
Uh, yeah...

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:30.290
Kosame, I'll get the car
ready to roll. Hurry and heal up.

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:32.330
Don't be ridiculous.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:39.200
All the cars other than Chase's are in shambles.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.910
We simply don't have the parts
or manpower to fix them.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:49.290
What's more, the only bridge that cars
can cross in the area was blown up...

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:52.540
...and the closest one is 300 kilometers south.

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:57.540
At the moment, I think
canceling the race is unavoidable.

00:17:57.540 --> 00:17:59.370
Canceled, huh?

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:03.250
As soon as my car is fixed, I'm rescuing Sofia.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:05.870
Do you know where Gil's at?

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:10.540
They left the train at a closed track
90 kilometers away.

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:14.660
They're probably hiding out
at a nearby ghost town.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.120
What about the ransom money?

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:22.910
I wish I could help, but it's not easy
to come up with 1.51 million.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:27.500
A ransom, huh? It's like Gil's
going out of his way.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:31.950
If he wanted that much,
robbing a bank or two would be quicker.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:35.250
It might not be money he's after.

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:38.500
In any case, it's risky to go empty-handed.

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:43.700
I can't wait. I promised Sofia
I would protect her.

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:47.250
Do you think you can fix your car?

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:50.080
If I can't, I'll ditch it and ride a horse.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.450
Don't ditch your car!

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:53.910
Huh?

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:01.620
Appare!

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.040
Al, I'll fix your car in a jiffy.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:08.870
But what about the missing parts?
My brake drum--

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:11.080
Forget your brakes.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.080
I'll give you new ones.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:17.290
Leave it to me.
I know everything about your car.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:20.700
In exchange, lend me all your mechanics.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:23.620
I'm fixing everyone's cars.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:29.120
After I do and we save Sofia by
kicking Gil's ass, the race is back on!

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.660
But the only bridge around is broken--

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:35.410
Who needs a bridge?
My car was originally a ship.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:36.950
Huh? But--

00:19:36.950 --> 00:19:41.830
There's no ifs or buts!
I'm not gonna let him get his way!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:49.660
The only way this race ends is when
one of us crosses the finish line.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.910
Stay behind if you're scared.

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:56.000
If you're fine with him stealing
all that's precious to you,

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.540
then you can stay right here.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:00.410
I'll just go alone!

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.000
You're not alone.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.410
I'm going, too.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:13.080
Us, too! Right, Bro?

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:16.080
Well, we ain't got much to lose.

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.410
I guess the race is back on.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.540
This time, I'll get serious.

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:25.830
Start by taking off that ugly mask.
It'll get in the way of fighting.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.000
My eyes shine too bright.

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:30.250
Moron.

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:36.250
Welcome back, Appare.

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.660
Stop, you're suffocating me.

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:43.120
Let's start by checking all the cars.
We'll make a list of parts--

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:44.580
Dammit!

00:20:46.160 --> 00:20:49.160
Here. There's your list of parts.

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:55.450
Gather all the craftsmen in the city!
We'll make the parts we need!

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:58.000
We're gonna fix every last car!

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.750
Including the other teams'?

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:05.450
Of course! Who gives a shit about teams?!
I won't let it end like this!

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:09.450
Spend as much as you must!
The responsibility's mine!

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:10.750
Understood.

00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:15.830
Start with Mr. Lyon's car! Show him
what GM engineers are made of!

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.000
Yes, sir!

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.370
I'm so fired.

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:23.620
Thanks, Seth.

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:26.450
Please, call me Al.

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:29.290
Al...

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:32.830
We're up against Gil. The police won't help.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:36.080
Are you fine with that, everyone?

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:39.580
I didn't expect them to help from the start.

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:42.410
We're outlaws, you know?

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.120
It's a mess.

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:49.790
Yeah, but it's okay.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:58.040
Hototo, can you hear its voice?

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:02.330
"I want to run farther! Make me go faster!"

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:08.790
Lend us your power. There's someone
out there waiting for us.

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:10.160
Appare...

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:13.950
Help me out. Just fixing it isn't much fun.

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:15.160
Huh?

